{{Quote|Razor Crest, M-One-Eleven. Come in, Razor Crest. Do you copy?|Carson Teva, to Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 10">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 10: The Passenger}}</ref>}}
The '''ST-70 assault ship''',<ref name="FFG">{{FFGXW2|set=Razor Crest Expansion Pack|cardname=The Mandalorian|ship=ST-70 Assault Ship}}</ref> also known as the '''ST-70 ''Razor Crest'' assault ship''' or simply as the '''ST-70 class''',<ref name="Encyclopedia">{{EncyclopediaCite|Miscellaneous Ships and Vehicles (1)}}</ref> was a class of [[gunship]]<ref name="Mandalorian Panel" /> manufactured by the [[Corellian Engineering Corporation]].<ref name="2024 Encyclopedia" /> Ships of the class were sometimes informally referred to as a "Razor Crest".<ref name="Return of the Mandalorian">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref> Its usage predated the [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="Chapter 1" /> when they were used for local military patrols.<ref name="Databank" /> One starship of this class was the similarly-named ''[[Razor Crest]]'', also designated M-111,<ref name="2024 Encyclopedia" /> the starship used by the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] during the [[New Republic Era]]<ref name="Chapter 1" /> in [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Mando Date">{{MandoDate|1}}</ref>

ST-70 Assault Ships had a single [[pilot]] and could hold at least four passengers.<ref name="Chapter 6" /> Two [[laser cannon]]s were equipped.<ref name="Chapter 5" /> ST-70s had two engines and a [[hyperdrive]].<ref name="Chapter 1" />

